# Build-context exclusions for infra/api/Dockerfile.
#
# BuildKit reads `<dockerfile-path>.dockerignore` in preference to the context
# root's `.dockerignore`, which lets the API image narrow the repository-root
# context without putting a root-level file in another agent's way.
#
# Rule of thumb: the API image needs the Python source, the two dependency
# manifests, and `packages/shared` (the cross-language book-table contract test
# reads books.data.ts from it). Everything else is dead weight — `node_modules/`
# alone is hundreds of megabytes and would be uploaded on every build.

# Everything is excluded by default; re-include only what the image needs.
*

!apps/api
!packages/shared
!requirements.txt
!requirements-dev.txt

# …minus the parts of those trees that must never enter an image.
apps/api/.venv
apps/api/.env
apps/api/.env.*
apps/api/**/__pycache__
apps/api/**/*.py[cod]
apps/api/**/.pytest_cache
apps/api/**/.ruff_cache
apps/api/**/.mypy_cache
packages/shared/node_modules
packages/shared/dist
